{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 1,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.406,
            0.071,
            0.813,
            0.089
          ],
          "content": "How Quantities Combine: Understanding Data"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.863,
            0.071,
            0.881,
            0.086
          ],
          "content": "9"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.11,
            0.882,
            0.151
          ],
          "content": "Method 1 does not work because it treats the average heights of seniors and of juniors equally — but there are many more seniors than juniors!"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.12,
            0.156,
            0.379,
            0.346
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_1_image_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.443,
            0.152,
            0.822,
            0.173
          ],
          "content": "Shreyas calculated it differently as"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.467,
            0.183,
            0.73,
            0.222
          ],
          "content": "\\frac{(165.5 \\times 8) + (149.33 \\times 3)}{8 + 3}",
          "image_source": "images/page_1_equation_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.468,
            0.247,
            0.705,
            0.317
          ],
          "content": "\\begin{aligned}=\\frac{1324 + 448}{11} &= \\frac{1772}{11} \\\\&= 161.09.\\end{aligned}",
          "image_source": "images/page_1_equation_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.443,
            0.327,
            0.876,
            0.348
          ],
          "content": "Do you understand why this also works?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.352,
            0.881,
            0.391
          ],
          "content": "Can you see why $1 6 5 . 5 \\times 8$ gives the sum of the heights of all the seniors and 149.33 × 3 gives the sum of the heights of all the juniors?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.392,
            0.881,
            0.432
          ],
          "content": "This phenomenon is explained below with a generalisation. Suppose we have two collections of data — Collection 1 and Collection 2."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.446,
            0.486,
            0.511
          ],
          "content": "Suppose the data in Collection 1, having n values, is $X_{1},X_{2},X_{3},\\ldots,X_{n}$ The average of Collection 1 is"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.508,
            0.446,
            0.883,
            0.489
          ],
          "content": "Suppose the data in Collection 2, having m values, is $y _ { 1 } , y _ { 2 } , y _ { 3 } , \\ldots , y _ { m }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.119,
            0.519,
            0.375,
            0.556
          ],
          "content": "\\frac{X_{_1} + X_{_2} + X_{_3} + \\cdots + X_{_n}}{n} = a.",
          "image_source": "images/page_1_equation_12.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.51,
            0.492,
            0.832,
            0.514
          ],
          "content": "The average of Collection 2 is"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.511,
            0.521,
            0.768,
            0.56
          ],
          "content": "\\frac{y_{1}+y_{2}+y_{3}+\\cdots+y_{m}}{m}=b.",
          "image_source": "images/page_1_equation_14.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.564,
            0.488,
            0.605
          ],
          "content": "Thus the sum of the data in Collection 1 is"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.509,
            0.567,
            0.811,
            0.606
          ],
          "content": "Thus the sum of the data in Collection 2 is"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.611,
            0.388,
            0.633
          ],
          "content": "X_{1} + X_{2} + X_{3} + \\cdots + X_{n} = an.",
          "image_source": "images/page_1_equation_17.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.512,
            0.613,
            0.789,
            0.636
          ],
          "content": "y_{1} + y_{2} + y_{3} + \\cdots + y_{m} = bm.",
          "image_source": "images/page_1_equation_18.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.641,
            0.617,
            0.662
          ],
          "content": "The average of the combined data is therefore"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.669,
            0.868,
            0.709
          ],
          "content": "(Sum of values in Collection 1) + (Sum of values in Collection 2) (Number of values in Collection 1) + (Number of values in Collection 2)"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.455,
            0.717,
            0.579,
            0.754
          ],
          "content": "\\operatorname { = } { \\frac { a n + b m } { n + m } } .",
          "image_source": "images/page_1_equation_21.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.774,
            0.535,
            0.909
          ],
          "content": "**Example 2:** Jaspreet recently learnt cycling. She has explored different routes in her town. She tracked how much time she cycled on weekdays over the last 3 weeks. Find the mean time spent cycling per weekday over the last 3 weeks."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.574,
            0.758,
            0.865,
            0.91
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_1_image_23.jpg"
        }
      ]
    }
